---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Nutrition"
  description="Meals and nutrition at Junior Hub Child Care & Learning Centre."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Nutrition and menu"
    lede="A hot lunch and two snacks every day, in a peanut-free kitchen."
    image="/images/carousel/Meal 1.jpg"
  ></PageHero>

  <div class="wrap page">
    <div class="prose">

      <p>
      Nutrition education and the promotion of healthy attitudes towards
      food are an important part of the care we provide for the children.
      A hot nutritious noon meal and two snacks (early morning and
      mid-afternoon) are provided daily for all children. As required by
      Health Canada and 2% M.F. milk as needed to toddler and preschool
      children at morning snack and lunch. Water will be served with the
      afternoon snack. Parents provide a water bottle, labeled with your
      child’s name, allowing ongoing access to water. Fresh fruit will
      also be available to the children at all times.</p>
      <p>JHCCLC provides meals that follow the guidelines of the Canada Food
      Guide. Weekly menus are posted on the Family Information Board and
      any alternatives are noted. Peanuts and peanut products are not used
      in any food preparation at this Centre.</p>
      <p>At least one staff member of JHCCLC will have successfully completed
      the examination based on York Region Public Health Ontario Ministry
      of Food Handler Training Protocol.</p>
      <p>The supervisor must be alerted to any food allergies, sensitives or
      restrictions upon enrolment. Substitutions, to the best of our
      ability, will be made to accommodate your child’s needs. In the
      event your child has a life-threatening allergy then the policy
      addressing anaphylactic protocol must be followed.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
